## **5.1 The four operational layers**

**Layer A — Presentation**

The user interacts with the application.

**Layer B — Control**

The application discovers devices, manages settings, communicates with DSP and supervises processes.

**Layer C — Audio processing**

The native audio engine performs actual processing.

**Layer D — Intelligence**

The analysis and AI services interpret the results and make recommendations.

The AI layer must not be in the critical real-time audio path. If the AI service is unavailable, the DSP engine must continue operating.

